   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWS7c",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "I believe New Zealand is at a critical precipice. I am asking for the party vote for NZ First because I believe everyday Kiwis deserve to be heard and represented by people that have walked a mile in their shoes and experienced firsthand many of the issues that concern them. Dunedin is in dire need of common-sense practical solutions to issues that require a full community response. We need more bold southern voices in Parliament!"
     },
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWSAR",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "As a Rural Registered Nurse, I worked on the front line of health care for over a decade. I understand what it means to advocate for both community and region and believe Dunedin needs greater representation in Central Government. I live and work in Dunedin, as an outreach advisor for Parliamentary services, so it's my job to connect our regions to the decision makers in Wellington who need to hear and understand our unique needs."
     },
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWSDG",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Address the cost-of-living crisis that is crippling our nation. Give young people a reason to stay."
     },
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWSG5",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Ensure there are jobs for all and education pathways to work and employment for our young people."
     },
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWSIu",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Ensure that accessible health care does not have a \"postcode\" and address shortfalls in funding."
     }
    ],
