   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWRZk",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "I'm running to stand up for Dunedin. Successive governments have taken us for granted - through cuts to the hospital rebuild and our tertiary sector. I've lived, studied and worked here, and I'm done watching it happen. This election you can change that: give me your electorate vote and the Greens your party vote, and we'll deliver real cost of living solutions, back our students and tertiary sector, and protect our climate and nature."
     },
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWRcZ",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "I have a proven record of delivering for Dunedin and creating change that people and planet need. In Parliament, I've asked more written questions than any other MP this term, and used them to expose Government cuts to Dunedin. As OUSA President, I delivered free breakfasts and student bus discounts, and brought town and gown together through student clean-up projects. At the Climate Commission, I led an ambitious plan to cut waste pollution and emissions."
     },
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWRfO",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Affordable lives: cheaper groceries (KiwiMart), cheaper power (KiwiPower) and first $10k tax free."
     },
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWRiD",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Back our students and tertiary sector: fees free, universal student allowance and real investment."
     },
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWRl2",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Protect nature and climate - stand up against fast track projects and invest in real climate action."
     }
    ],
